Staged, not yet described. Organizing: no sidecar of its own, holds no role.

Three stand-ins for what actually accumulates here, per SAT Sidecars: Config and Metadata v0.0.13's list of what belongs beneath an organizing directory: a database export feeding an ingress process (legacy-site-export.csv), a scanned original capture (scans/2024-intake-001.txt, standing in for a real scan), and a working draft that is not yet, and may never be, a resource (draft-notes.md). None of the three has a sidecar. draft-notes.md deliberately carries a .md extension to make the point plainly: the constraint on an organizing directory is what is in it, not what it is named or shaped like. A file here is not a node until someone gives it one.
